OL,3,GNEWSACancer patient does 100th parkrun
OL,4,Aafter transplant
OL,5,
OL,6,FA blood cancer patient has celebrated
OL,7,Frunning his 100th parkrun, a year to
OL,8,Fthe day after he had a stem cell
OL,9,Ftransplant.
OL,11,FJohn Osborn from Paignton was supported
OL,12,Fto do the run by staff at Torbay
OL,13,FHospital, where he has been in a
OL,14,Fclinical trial offering patients more
OL,15,Fpersonalised treatment plans.
OL,17,FHis diagnosis with myeloma, a type of
OL,18,Fcancer that affects the blood and bone
OL,19,Fmarrow, came after his back and pelvis
OL,20,Fstarted hurting after running.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,347,340,200,160,0,100
